data live_tree_disposition: LiveTreeDisposition = SubstrateInputsOnly

// THE SUBJECT IS THE CANDIDATE FIELD OF A REAL SPILL POPULATION, AND THE POPULATION IS UNEVEN ON
// PURPOSE BECAUSE THE REAL ONE IS.
//
// The CI spill roster names four compute offers - a Scaleway AMP2 instance, a Hetzner CAX41, an
// Oracle Ampere A1 and a GCP N2 on-demand instance. Exactly one of those four providers has a route
// whose data paths anybody has modeled. Three do not, and the question this file answers is what
// happens to the other three: whether an offer whose provider we have never assessed is refused,
// or whether it quietly reaches the ranking and wins on price because nothing was there to stop it.
//
// WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT ASSERT ABOUT ANY REAL VENDOR, stated first because getting this wrong is
// worse than the coverage gap it would paper over. The four offer IDENTITIES are real - those are
// products that exist and that our own spill roster names. THE ROUTE FACTS BELOW ARE NOT A READING
// OF ANY VENDOR'S SUBPROCESSOR DOCUMENTATION, DATA-RESIDENCY REPRESENTATIONS OR CONTRACT. They are
// this witness's declared inputs, and every one of them cites a row in this module that says so in
// its own text. DESIGN section 4d's rule is that a figure carries its evidentiary standing in the
// type rather than in a reader's memory; the standing of everything here is "witness input, read
// obligation outstanding", and the obligation is named. Nobody may cite this file as evidence that
// Hetzner's execution path is located where this file puts it - the whole point of the file is that
// the corpus has not read those paths for three of four providers.
//
// THE FOURTH IS A DIFFERENT STATE AND THE DIFFERENCE MATTERS, because writing it down wrongly is
// how somebody is sent to do a read that has already been done. A Hetzner read EXISTS and is owned:
// six dated published-source readings, one of them a NEGATIVE reading recording what the vendor's
// technical-and-organizational-measures page does not say. It is UNLANDED rather than missing, and
// deliberately so - it is sequenced behind a carrier change that widens ProviderPathUnread with a
// consulted slot, so that an unread path can cite the documents that were consulted and failed to
// answer. Carrier first, census conforms. This witness therefore does not reach for those readings
// because they are not in this tree yet, not because nobody has done the work.
//
// WHY THE ONE MODELED ROUTE IS ALSO THE DEAREST. Scaleway is priced lowest and Hetzner highest, so
// the surviving offer is the one that loses on every economic axis. If compliance were a conjunct
// beside cost - or a tiebreak, or a penalty added to a total - the cheap unassessed offer would win
// and this file would go red. It wins nothing, because it is never in the list the ranker is
// handed.
//
// THE PRICES ARE ORDINALS, NOT QUOTES. They are 1000, 2000, 3000 and 4000 micros an hour, spaced so
// the ORDER is unmistakable and so no reader can mistake them for a vendor's published rate. The
// subject of every claim below is which offer survives, never what anything costs; a real quote
// belongs to a pricing authority and is cited from there, never transcribed into a witness.

// ── THE POPULATION'S ROUTE COMPONENTS, DECLARED SO EVERY CITATION RESOLVES ────────────────────
//
// The provider and service components of the Hetzner route cite extdeps.cloud.hetzner, which is the
// real upstream authority for that vendor and already carries its catalog. The REGION component
// cites a row in this module instead, and the reason is a real modeling state rather than laziness:
// that module models regions as a closed coproduct (HetznerCloudRegion = Helsinki | Nuremberg) with
// no per-region DECLARATION to name, and DESIGN section 3 requires citing a symbol rather than a
// position, so there is presently nothing upstream to point at. TRIGGER: a per-region declaration in
// extdeps.cloud.hetzner, at which point this row is deleted and the citation moves upstream.
data spill_hetzner_helsinki_region: NonEmptyStr = "spill-hetzner-region-helsinki"
data spill_hetzner_nuremberg_region: NonEmptyStr = "spill-hetzner-region-nuremberg"
// THE EXERCISE RECEIPT every witness route exercise cites. Like the region rows it is this witness's
// declared input, not a reading of any real run on any real vendor.
data spill_route_exercise: NonEmptyStr = "spill-route-exercise-witness-input"

// THE THREE PROVIDERS WITH NO MODELED ROUTE. NO ROUTE FACTS ARE MODELED FOR ANY OF THESE THREE
// ANYWHERE IN THIS CORPUS: no data-path closure, no downstream population, no contract terms. That
// is the population's actual state and is the subject of this file, not an omission in it.
//
// The rows exist so the OFFERS can name the route they claim to run on - an offer must state its
// route or a facts row could never be found to disagree with it - and they deliberately carry no
// facts. Naming a provider here establishes nothing whatever about that provider.
//
// THE VALUES ARE IDENTIFIERS AND THE PROSE IS HERE, which is DESIGN section 4c rather than a style
// choice: an ordinary String declaration whose purpose is commentary is misplaced data, mechanically
// indistinguishable from program data, and "//" is the quarantine boundary the corpus settled on
// after sweeping 215 such rows. The sibling rows this file sits beside - the live probe's
// probe_customer_profile, the admission fixture's fixture_provider - are identifier-shaped for the
// same reason.
data spill_scaleway_provider: NonEmptyStr = "spill-provider-scaleway"
data spill_scaleway_service: NonEmptyStr = "spill-service-scaleway-amp2"
data spill_scaleway_region: NonEmptyStr = "spill-region-scaleway-unread"
data spill_oracle_provider: NonEmptyStr = "spill-provider-oracle"
data spill_oracle_service: NonEmptyStr = "spill-service-oci-ampere-a1"
data spill_oracle_region: NonEmptyStr = "spill-region-oci-unread"
data spill_google_provider: NonEmptyStr = "spill-provider-google"
data spill_google_service: NonEmptyStr = "spill-service-gce-n2-on-demand"
data spill_google_region: NonEmptyStr = "spill-region-gcp-unread"

// ── THE WITNESS'S DECLARED INPUTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// THE READ IS OUTSTANDING IN THIS TREE. No route facts here state any of these providers' data-path
// closures - execution, durable storage, backups, logs, telemetry, control plane, support access,
// administrative access and spill - nor enumerate their downstream providers. For one of the four
// providers such a read has been performed and is awaiting a carrier change before it lands; for
// the other three none exists. Either way it is not HERE, so until a real reading lands and is
// cited to the provider's own published representations, every path standing built from these rows
// is an INPUT TO A TEST and is not a fact about any provider.
//
// spill_witness_read_obligation is what every ProviderPathLocated arm below cites as its evidence,
// so the obligation is not a note beside the data - it is the DeclarationRef the typed carrier
// points at, reachable from any path standing this witness constructs.
data spill_witness_read_obligation: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-read-obligation"
data spill_witness_operator: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-operator"
data spill_witness_jurisdiction: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-jurisdiction"
data spill_witness_no_spill_path: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-no-spill-path"
data spill_witness_no_downstream: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-no-downstream"
data spill_witness_contract_terms: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-contract-terms"
data spill_witness_posture_authority: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-posture-authority"
data spill_witness_customer_profile: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-customer-profile"
data spill_witness_data_handling_profile: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-data-handling-profile"
data spill_witness_agreement: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-agreement"
data spill_witness_prohibited_use_cleared: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-prohibited-use-cleared"
data spill_witness_sanctions_cleared: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-sanctions-cleared"
data spill_witness_export_cleared: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-export-cleared"
data spill_witness_decision_receipt: NonEmptyStr = "spill-witness-decision-receipt"

fn s_hash(seed: String) -> ContentHash {
  as_content_hash_structural(structural: content_hash_atom(value: seed))
}

